{#
    A picture on its own — `.. image::`, which is a figure with nothing claimed
    under it.

    The core writes a bare `<img>` into the prose. A picture on the page
    ground with no edge around it is the same failure `figure.html.twig`
    exists to stop. A drawing exported on white sits in a hole in dark. One
    that does not fill its column has nothing that says where it ends. So
    the node comes out as `sds-figure` too. The frame, the ground and
    `sds-art` have one decision, for everything that shows a picture.

    What it does not get is a caption, and that is the whole difference between
    the two directives. A figure is a picture an author made a claim about, an
    image is one they dropped in. The element draws the frame without one.

    Dropped in is also why the SVG under an `.. image::` is the one least
    likely to exist for this system at all. It does not have to. The picture
    is a link, so whatever is in the file is what arrives.

    `:target:` stays a link around the picture, where the core put it as well.
    `:zoomable:` opens it at full size and is the author's to write. `:align:`
    and `:title:` drop out — a column this narrow has nothing to float beside,
    and a tooltip is a label only a mouse can read.
#}
{%- set source = node.value is external_target ? node.value : asset(node.value) -%}
{%- if node.target %}<a href="{{ node.target.url }}">{% endif -%}
<sds-figure
    src="{{ source }}"
    alt="{{ node.option('alt')|default('') }}"
    {%- if node.hasOption('width') %} width="{{ node.option('width') }}"{% endif -%}
    {%- if node.hasOption('height') %} height="{{ node.option('height') }}"{% endif -%}
    {#- Opens at full size where the author asked for it, and nowhere else.
        Most pictures in a document read at the width they stand in. Never
        under a `:target:` — that link is already around the whole picture, and
        the press is a second anchor inside it. -#}
    {%- if node.hasOption('zoomable') and not node.target %} zoomable{% endif -%}
    {%- if node.classesString %} class="{{ node.classesString }}"{% endif -%}
></sds-figure>
{%- if node.target %}</a>{% endif -%}
